preConditionHook:
// Brooks's two-bar reversal, read as one signal bar: a bear trend bar followed by a
// bull bar of comparable size that closes back above the bear bar's MIDPOINT.
// Four terms of two-bar OHLC arithmetic, no state, so both conditions are
// written out and there is nothing for a hook to hold.
//
// The midpoint is (high[1] + low[1]) / 2 -- the bar's range midpoint, not its
// body midpoint; the body-midpoint reading (T11-05) is a variant that was not
// carried. The size term is a plain range ratio, so a doji second bar of the
// right size still qualifies -- the body test lives in TrendBarBody /
// StrongTrendBar as a separate placement.
//
// The divisor is the constant 2, never zero, so no epsilon guard is needed
// against EasyLanguage's runtime divide-by-zero.
// Every comparison is one EasyLanguage relational, so el_gt / el_lt / el_ge.
